+\ 18.11 (experiment): words whose definition the emulator holds (op HOST, emulator/src/proto.def).
+\ A call: the arguments go to the cells of %HA, the request record of the word (constant, written once by
+\ %HINIT) is copied to the channel SYS, the emulator runs the C definition at once and writes the result to
+\ the cell 0 of %HA. Compiled before everything else, in the kernel; the host pForth does not see it.
+\ The memory of the kernel (its "Forth addresses") starts at the bit 1619001344 = 3 * 2^29 + 2^23.
+create %hq 64 allot
+create %ha 16 allot
+%hq 16 * 1619001344 + constant %hr0
+%hr0 256 + constant %hr1
+: %hcall0 ( -- ) 2147483648 2147483648 %hr0 %hr0 152 + %copy ;
+: %hcall1 ( -- ) 2147483648 2147483648 %hr1 %hr1 152 + %copy ;
+\ The record (152 bits, numeric, byte by byte): op 8, chan 32, flags 16, arg 32, off 64.
+: %hw1 ( at v -- at' ) over dup 8 + spacec! 8 + ;
+: %hn ( at v n -- at' ) 0 ?do dup 255 and >r 8 rshift swap r> %hw1 swap loop drop ;
+: %hrec ( k at -- ) swap >r 7 1 %hn 1619001344 4 %hn 0 2 %hn r> 4 %hn %ha 4 %hn 0 4 %hn drop ;
+: %hinit ( -- ) 0 %hr0 %hrec 1 %hr1 %hrec ;
+%hinit
+: fill ( addr u c -- ) %ha 8 + ! %ha 4 + ! %ha ! %hcall1 ;
